# Cloudflare Workers assets ignore file (wrangler-native, gitignore syntax, relative to the assets dir root).
# Files matched here are excluded from the upload manifest. Copied into out/ from public/ at build time, the
# same way _headers and _redirects are.
#
# Next 16 emits ~8 per-segment client-cache prefetch payloads ("__next.*") for every prerendered route. The
# /talk/[topic] boards enumerate the full, finite astrology vocabulary (707 topics x 4 locales), so those
# segment files alone are ~22,600 files and push the export past Cloudflare's 20,000-file asset limit on the
# free plan. They are a pure client-navigation optimization: the crawlable <topic>.html shell (with baked
# comments) and the full <topic>.txt RSC payload are kept, and the Next client falls back to <topic>.txt — or
# a full-document nav to <topic>.html — when a segment file is absent. Excluding them keeps the deploy far
# under the limit and bounded forever (the vocabulary is finite). Segment files outside /talk (home, love,
# today) are NOT matched, so those high-traffic pages keep their instant per-segment prefetch.
**/talk/**/__next.*
